          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life and Academic Career</strong><br>\nWoodrow Wilson was born on December 28, 1856, in Staunton, Virginia. Before entering politics, he had a distinguished career in academia, serving as the president of Princeton University and governor of New Jersey.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Presidential Election</strong><br>\nWilson was elected the 28th President of the United States in 1912 after serving as Governor of New Jersey. His campaign promised a progressive agenda called the New Freedom, which aimed to promote antitrust modification, tariff reform, and improvements in banking.</p>\n\n<p><strong>New Freedom Reforms</strong><br>\nDuring his first term, Wilson accomplished significant reforms, including the Federal Reserve Act, which created a central banking system, and the Clayton Antitrust Act, which strengthened previous antitrust laws to better control big business.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 4.415011037527593,
            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>World War I Leadership</strong><br>\nWilson initially kept the United States neutral during World War I. However, in 1917, he asked Congress to declare war on Germany, stating that the world must be made safe for democracy, marking the U.S. entry into the conflict.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Fourteen Points and the League of Nations</strong><br>\nIn 1918, Wilson presented his Fourteen Points, a statement of principles for peace that was to be used for peace negotiations to end World War I. The most significant point was the establishment of the League of Nations, an international organization designed to prevent future conflicts.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Paris Peace Conference</strong><br>\nAs the war concluded, Wilson played a prominent role in the Paris Peace Conference of 1919. He worked to promote his vision of a peace settlement that would prevent such destruction from happening again.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
